    "mean_decode_tokens_per_sec": "Mean, over successful requests with at least two tokens, of (output_tokens - 1) / (time from the first token to the last token).",
    "measurement_window_s": "On the run clock, earliest measured request issue to latest measured request finish at that concurrency level. Warmup is outside the window. The load pattern is closed-loop: at most `concurrency` requests are in flight, and a new request starts when a slot frees. Client-side queue delay is not part of latency. Queueing inside the server still appears in TTFT.",
    "output_tokens": "Count of non-empty streamed pieces delivered to the client. This follows the provider's stream tokenization and is not a local retokenization.",
